# Core's versioned execution-profile registry, as federated to this package.
# The data (`.nirs4all_execution_profiles_lines`) is generated by
# nirs4all-core/scripts/generate_capability_profiles.py from
# compat/capabilities.toml and embedded in execution_profiles_data.R; this file
# only decodes it. R is NOT a Core runtime surface: the registry records R as
# an externally federated surface whose contracts and evidence live here.

#' Native execution profiles and the R federation record
#'
#' Returns the profile registry published by nirs4all-core
#' (`nirs4all-core.execution-profiles.v1`). It declares five native profiles at
#' version 1: `native-workflow@1`, `native-conformal@1`, `native-methods-package@1`,
#' `native-n4a-canonical@1` and `n4a-container@1`, with per-operation
#' `supported`/`unsupported` entries (compile, fit, predict, import, export) for
#' each Core runtime surface, per-surface runtime requirements, and the current
#' content declared per operation, surface and route (`content_routes`): which
#' route returns a host object, which carries the Core wrapper JSON schema id
#' `nirs4all.calibrated.v1`, and which transfers the native archive V2 bytes.
#' `external_federation` holds the record for this package, which is outside
#' Core's runtime surfaces and references those five profiles. The entries
#' are a metadata contract: readability, execution support and scientific
#' qualification are separate, and it is not a numerical certification.
#' @return A fresh list decoded from the embedded registry; modifying it never
#'   changes later calls.
#' @export
nirs4all_execution_profiles <- function() {
  jsonlite::fromJSON(paste(.nirs4all_execution_profiles_lines, collapse = "\n"),
                     simplifyVector = FALSE)
}
